Drop MSYS2 packages removed from mingw64

Purpose: keep the Windows installer build working. MSYS2 removed
mingw-w64-x86_64-diffutils and mingw-w64-x86_64-desktop-file-utils,
so 'just prerequisites-win' fails before anything is built.

Approach: drop both from the pacman list. Nothing needs diffutils;
meson looks for desktop-file-validate with required: false.

Constraints: temporary. Upstream is moving the Windows build to
ucrt64 (branch flxzt/win-ucrt64); delete this patch once that lands.
